#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# csch

#% text
# `csch(x)` gives the hyperbolic cosecant 1/sinh(x).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `csch(x)` stays unevaluated for symbolic `x`; where `sinh(x)` has an exact value, `csch(x)` is its reciprocal.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% item
# `csch` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
csch(im*pi/2)
#% output
#= -1im

#% cell
csch(1.0)
#% output
#= 0.8509181282393216

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Symbolic arguments and symmetry:

#% cell
csch(-x)
#% output
#= -csch(x)

#% text
# 30 digits:

#% cell
n(csch(1), 30)
#% output
#= 0.8509181282393215451338427632871753

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `sinh`, `sin`, `cos`, `tan`
